            <ArticleTitle>[Acute pelvic pain in women].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1657-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute pelvic pains in women can reflect highly diverse disorders of varying severity, sometimes requiring surgery. It thus is clearly a part of abdominal emergencies in the adult. Good knowledge of underlying gynaecological disorders usually avoids unnecessary surgery. The use of echography has greatly contributed to reducing coelioscopy for diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
